mvvault: checkpoint 6 should keep the earlier checkpoints' tests

For gabeorlanski/scb-problems (main, 4d38d30). Not applied to the cache here: every run
so far scored checkpoint 6 the upstream way, and flipping it would make new runs
incomparable. To try it, apply to a copy and point SCBENCH_PROBLEMS_PATH at it.

Checkpoints 2 to 5 of mvvault set include_prior_tests: true and checkpoint 6 sets it
false, so the last checkpoint runs only its own 42 tests (5 core, 23 functionality, 14
error) and none of the 185 from checkpoints 1 to 5. A run that carries misses through
five checkpoints is then "strict" on the sixth for free: the Opus 5 just-solve control
scored 35/37, 64/67, 110/115, 149/155, 179/185 and then 42/42, its one strict
checkpoint. The README says tests for checkpoint N assume all prior checkpoints still
pass, and checkpoint 6's spec (annotations, with auto-migration of v1 and v2 vaults to
v3) extends the earlier behaviour rather than replacing it. The reference solution
agrees: evaluated as checkpoint 6 with prior tests on, solutions/checkpoint_6 passes
5/5 core, 23/23 functionality, 14/14 error and 185/185 regression (scb eval-snapshot,
2026-09-08).

--- a/mvvault/config.yaml
+++ b/mvvault/config.yaml
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
     version: 2
     order: 6
     state: Core Tests
-    include_prior_tests: false
+    include_prior_tests: true
 
 test_dependencies:
   - httpx
